    "check": "returned unopposed, no poll; every name checked against the page image"
  },
  "note": "Nominations were announced by V. M. Conran, town clerk, at Armagh City Hall on Wednesday 4 May: eighteen candidates for the twenty seats, so there was no contest in any ward. Mrs Catherine Agnew was the first woman member of the council; P. Agnew had led the Independent Labour opposition on the old council, and the ward's members now sat as the Eire Labour Party. Polling day for the urban councils was Wednesday 18 May 1949 (Belfast News-Letter, 19 May 1949, p. 5: \"Polling took place yesterday for the election of county borough, borough and urban councils in Ulster\")."
